INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('Prose', 255, 'story', '1064', '- **PRS-US-Q8 ✅** As the maintainer, I clean up Epic H stories PRS-US-H9..H12 and their children (H9a..H12g; H9e..H9h are planned) so the backlog matches the novel factory and states only what is true. Rules to apply (sources: docs/rfc/0015-novel-factory.md, the SessionStart forbidden list, SS-LAW-17): (1) THE PLAN IS THE FACTORY — book work is computed by the Hub (prose --factory next / --order list), never stored as story text, so a story that tracks chapters, acts, word counts or beats of a book is restated as a pointer to the factory or marked superseded; (2) THE BOOK IS THE BOOK — no outline, spine, ledger, summary or reconciler; (3) no LLM judges, review panels, votes or review-score thresholds (≥85% etc.); (4) RESULTS NOT TOOLS — a story is done only when its effect is applied and verified, never because a tool exists; (5) every ✅ cites a test or CLI check that exists today. For each story: show it (workflow story show <ID>); grep src/Prose.UnitTests for every cited test and run them (dotnet test --filter); a ✅ whose evidence is missing or failing drops to partial with the gap stated; rewrite (workflow story edit) any text that asks for a forbidden thing; mark a story that the factory now owns as done-superseded with a pointer. Touch no prose, no canon, no DB outside the workflow CLI. Then run workflow db render, commit the regenerated docs/USER_STORIES.md and list each story changed and why in the ticket.');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('Prose', 256, 'story', '1065', '- **PRS-US-Q9 ⬜** As the maintainer, every story ID in the Prose backlog is unique. PRS-US-H7 and H7a, H7b, H7c each exist twice in the workflow database. Compare each pair with workflow story show; if they say the same thing, merge into one; if they differ, renumber the later one to the next free ID in epic H. Then workflow db render, check that docs/USER_STORIES.md has no duplicate IDs, and commit. BLOCKED 2026-10-15: the workflow CLI has no command to renumber or delete a story and `db check` does not report duplicate IDs, so this needs a MindAttic.Workflow change first (`story renumber`, duplicate-ID check). After renumbering, give both H7 stories the same factory note as the other epic-H books (PRS-US-Q7): Rook Trilogy = MxG F5 fails 3/3, NxR F5 fails 1/4, CxC F5 fails 3/3 (PRS-T77); Steppin Razor (SRZR) F5 fails 3/3, F1 waiting (PRS-T77); mark both partial and their review-score children historical.');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('Prose', 257, 'story', '1066', '- **PRS-US-Q10 ⬜** As the author, every remaining GLMZ book is fully tagged, read and verified: work open tickets PRS-T56..PRS-T68 one book per run, in order, each to its own done criteria (factory F1-F7 green for that book), closing each ticket as it lands. Story is done when all thirteen are closed.');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('Prose', 258, 'story', '1067', '- **PRS-US-Q11 ⬜** As the author, every book in the other universes (SCRY, NONFICTION, FICTION, HORROR, EROTICA, GOSPEL, EVE, ANTHOLOGY) is fully tagged, read and verified. PRS-T69..PRS-T76 listed each universe''s books and expanded into one ticket per real book (PRS-T84..PRS-T103; EROTICA has no books, so PRS-T73 closed with nothing to expand); work each per-book ticket to factory F1-F7 green. Done when every non-calibration book''s factory status is green.');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('Prose', 259, 'story', '1068', '- **PRS-US-Q12 ⬜** As the author, no pressed book carries un-read beats after later record edits: work ticket PRS-T77 (final re-read, F1 recommit, re-export) after PRS-US-Q10 and PRS-US-Q11 are done.');
INSERT INTO blocks (repo, ordinal, kind, ref, text) VALUES ('Prose', 260, 'story', '1069', '- **PRS-US-Q13 ⬜** As the author, the GLMZ focus wheel''s cycle 2 is a full re-read of every catalog book (the change-tracking dockets select.py needs to do the cheap diff were lost with a prior session''s scratchpad, so this cycle falls back to wheel rule 2: a whole-book read). Each of the 22 books (SCON excluded) gets its own ticket: read the focus book in full against the current text of all 21 others, draft only meaningful rows (cold-reader gaps, consequences, behavior, veracity, belonging), borrow capped at 3 rows/zero normal, reject re-litigated rulings or invented source facts, then archive+splice+tag+capture+re-read the changed beats+F1 verify. Done when every book''s ticket is closed and prose --factory status is clean for all 22.');
